  "translation": "Last weekend, my mother and I set out from home together to go shopping. We took the bus to the mall. The mall was very crowded, so we first looked around the bookstore on the left side of the second floor. There was a book about cooking that I liked the most because I can cook. Mother asked me what book I was buying, and I said this book was really not expensive, but I didn't need it. Then we went to the basement floor of this supermarket; I often come to this supermarket to buy things. Inside the supermarket, we saw apples and bananas. Mother asked me whether I wanted apples or bananas. I said I wanted apples, and she asked me how many to buy; I said three. She also bought four eggs, and we did not buy those bananas. We also bought a piece of bread and a glass of milk, and also bought half a piece of chocolate. We were queuing to pay. At checkout, the cashier said the total was 62 yuan. Mother could not use her phone to pay, so she gave her 100 yuan. She gave 38 yuan change. Holding our things, we all happily went home, deciding to come again next time."
